{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1705","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Mark and the Online Exam"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mark is administering an online exam consisting of $$$n$$$ true-false questions. However, he has lost all answer keys. He needs a way to retrieve the answers before his client gets infuriated."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Fortunately, he has access to the grading system. Thus, for each query, you can input the answers to all $$$n$$$ questions, and the grading system will output how many of them are correct."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"He doesn't have much time, so he can use the grading system at most $$$675$$$ times. Help Mark determine the answer keys."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that answer keys are fixed in advance and will not change depending on your queries."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input consists of an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\leq n\\leq 1000$$$) — the number of questions."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"custom","title":"Interaction"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After reading $$$n$$$, you can start making queries to the grading system. For each query, print a line containing a string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$ consisting of only letters '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s_i = $$$'"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' means that you answer the $$$i$$$-question "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s_i = $$$'"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' means that you answer the $$$i$$$-question "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After a successful query, you should read an integer $$$k$$$ ($$$0\\leq k\\leq n$$$) — the number of correct answers. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If you read $$$n$$$, then you found the answers, and your program should not make any more queries."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If your program reads $$$k = -1$$$ instead of the number of correct answers, it means that you either made an invalid query or exceeded the query limits. Exit immediately after receiving $$$-1$$$, and you will see "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Wrong answer"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" verdict. Otherwise, you can get an arbitrary verdict because your solution will continue to read from a closed stream."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After printing a query do not forget to output end of line and flush the output. Otherwise, you will get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Idleness limit exceeded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". To do this, use: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fflush(stdout)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in C++; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"System.out.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Java; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flush(output)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Pascal; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"stdout.flush()"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in Python; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" see documentation for other languages. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hacks"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To hack, use the following format:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\leq n\\leq 1000$$$) — the number of questions."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$ consisting of only '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' — the answer key."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n\n1\n\n3"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n\nFTT\n\nTTF\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n\n0\n\n3\n\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n\nFTFF\n\nTTTT\n\nTFTT\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The empty lines in the example are just for you to better understand the interaction process. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You're not required to print them."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, there are $$$3$$$ questions, and the answer to each question is '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', respectively. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The first query, guessing the answers to be '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', respectively, guesses only one question — the $$$2$$$-nd question — correctly. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Then, in the second query, the program correctly guesses the answer key. The interaction ends here. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, there are $$$4$$$ questions, and the answer to each question is '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', and '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"', respectively. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The first query guessed none of the questions correctly, resulting in the answer $$$0$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The second query guessed the $$$1$$$-st, $$$3$$$-rd, and $$$4$$$-th question correctly, resulting in the answer $$$3$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" In the third query, the program correctly guesses the answer key. Then, the interaction ends. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1705F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1705/problem/F"}